\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {II}{\ignorespaces Test results on three MVTec AD categories. I-JEPA-AD uses adaptive masking with $\lambda =1$ and either the default gate ($\tau =0.5$) or the gate calibrated on nominal validation images (0.99 token quantile, $\tau \approx 0.16$--$0.35$; the setting declared as primary before test scoring). ``Image AUROC'' uses the max patch score and ``top-5'' the top-5 mean score. Augmented rows use the default gate. The PatchCore-style row is a nearest-neighbour reference on the same latents, not a full PatchCore. Best value per column and category in bold.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
