\newlabel{fig:heat}{{3}{5}{}{figure.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Hazelnut crack with the default and the calibrated gate (baseline predictor). The cyan contour is the ground truth. With the calibrated gate ($\tau =0.350$) the fine pass fires on 32 tokens around the defect (48 masks in total instead of 16) and the fused map suppresses background clutter. Each panel is min-max normalised for display only; pixel AUROC is computed per image on the raw map. This is the one example where the calibrated gate helped clearly; see the text for the other two.}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:hazcal}{{4}{5}{}{figure.4}{}}
