\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {VII}{\ignorespaces Test results after the validation-selected changes (official test split, one scoring pass per row). All layer-32 rows use the same predictor architecture, training recipe and masks as the baseline; only the cached tokens change. Image AUROC is given for the max score and for the mean of the top-3 token scores. The z-score settings (position z-score, $k{=}3$) were chosen on synthetic validation defects for the final-layer predictor and carried over unchanged; layer 32 was chosen on the same synthetic data. \textsuperscript  {a}Re-selected on layer-32 synthetic validation data and scored once on test; its score is the max (top-3 shown for comparison only). \textsuperscript  {b}Nearest-neighbour reference on layer-32 tokens (full memory bank), context only.}}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
